# Build-context filter for the Dockerfile: an ALLOWLIST. Everything is out unless named below. Two jobs: keep
# secrets and state out of the daemon (a context can leak .env, data/ or a docker/secrets file into a layer),
# and keep the context to what the build reads, so the transfer is small and a COPY only changes on a real
# source change. A denylist leaked whatever a checkout grew next: before this, the gitignored codegraph index
# (826 MB) and stale dist/ build output went into each build (measured 2026-10-03: a 930 MB context, now
# about 0.5 MB).
# A file the build needs and this list misses fails the build loudly, at the COPY or the step that reads it.
*

# the workspace: manifests, lockfile, patches (a frozen install refuses to run without them), and the sources
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!patches/
!packages/
!tooling/
# vite and the packages' tsconfig `extends` read the root configs
!tsconfig*.json
# the root `prepare` lifecycle script and the version-stamp entry (assemble-runtime.sh)
!scripts/prepare.ts
!scripts/build-version-stamp.ts
# the two files from docker/ the image uses
!docker/assemble-runtime.sh
!docker/entrypoint.sh

# The four plain-text ref files the version stamp reads to stamp /app/version.json (the build identity every
# surface reports — docker/assemble-runtime.sh). No objects, no history, no packfiles: HEAD plus the loose
# branch/tag refs plus the packed table. Measured on this repo 2026-09-18: HEAD 21 B, packed-refs ~14.4 KiB,
# refs/heads ~861 B over 21 files, refs/tags 0 — well under 16 KiB total. Without these the image can only
# report `unknown` for its own commit, which is the exact thing a bug report needs.
!.git/HEAD
!.git/refs/heads/**
!.git/refs/tags/**
!.git/packed-refs

# Generated or local inside the allowed trees: rebuilt in the image, or never part of it.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.cpuprofile
**/*.log
